    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.2.5: Lark grammar frontend; sparse FSM end states (removes quadratic FSM-construction memory); prevent XML whitespace state explosion; plus 0.2.4 fixes. Source now generated from the git tag via _service (upstream dropped the PyPI sdist; C++ build needs bundled 3rdparty submodules). %check smoke test temporarily tolerates the transformers ImportError caused by the current Factory python-transformers 5.14.1 (tokenizers&lt;=0.23.0) vs python-tokenizers 0.23.1 skew, while still asserting the native C++ binding loads.</comment>
    <requestid>1367538</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="3" vrev="2">
    <srcmd5>fc7b24092bb84697d36d25422c8f7cf2</srcmd5>
    <version>0.2.5</version>
    <time>1788518421</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Forward the stranded devel-only reproducibility fix (no version change, still 0.2.5):
exclude the static libxgrammar.a and the headers from the wheel via
SKBUILD_WHEEL_EXCLUDE instead of deleting them in %install, so dist-info/RECORD no
longer retains the varying checksum of the unreproducible fat-LTO static library.
Accepted into science:machinelearning on 2026-08-18 (rq1371724) but never forwarded.

Upstream v0.2.5.post1 was deliberately not taken: it is a PyPI-wheel-matrix
re-release whose only source delta vs v0.2.5 is the version string in
pyproject.toml plus a GitHub Actions change, so it is a no-op for this package,
which builds from the git tag.</comment>
    <requestid>1375572</requestid>
  </revision>
